---
// FILE: privacy.astro
// Purpose: Privacy & Secrets Policy page detailing ODS local-first architecture, zero telemetry, and secrets isolation.
// Layer: Marketing page

import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy & Secrets Policy — Open Document Spec (ODS)"
  description="Open Document Spec (ODS) is built with a local-first, zero-telemetry, and strict secrets isolation architecture. Read our full Privacy & Secrets Policy."
  activeNav="home"
>
  <div class="privacy-container">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="privacy-header">
      <div class="header-badge">
        <span class="badge-dot"></span>
        SECURITY & DATA PROTECTION
      </div>
      <h1 class="privacy-title">Privacy & Secrets Policy</h1>
      <p class="privacy-subtitle">
        Open Document Spec (ODS) is engineered with a strict <strong>Local-First</strong>, <strong>Zero-Telemetry</strong>, and <strong>Share-Aware Isolation</strong> architecture. Your documentation, code, and workspace data never leave your environment.
      </p>

      <div class="meta-pills">
        <span class="meta-pill">✓ 100% Local Processing</span>
        <span class="meta-pill">✓ Zero Remote Telemetry</span>
        <span class="meta-pill">✓ Share-Aware Visibility (<code>share: private</code>)</span>
        <span class="meta-pill">✓ Apache 2.0 Licensed</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <hr class="privacy-divider" />

    <!-- Main Content Body -->
    <main class="privacy-content">
      <!-- Section 1: Executive Summary -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>1. Executive Summary & Core Guarantees</h2>
        <p>
          Open Document Spec (ODS) provides automated Markdown index management, graph link repair, and AI context resolution. We believe developer tools must respect codebase privacy and data sovereignty above all else.
        </p>
        <div class="guarantee-cards">
          <div class="guarantee-card">
            <h3>🔒 Local-First Engine</h3>
            <p>All indexing, link repair, schema validation, and graph operations execute 100% locally on your CPU via the compiled Rust binary (<code>ods</code>). No code or prose is ever sent to external cloud servers.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="guarantee-card">
            <h3>🚫 Zero Telemetry & Tracking</h3>
            <p>ODS contains zero analytics, tracking beacons, error monitoring reporting, or phone-home telemetry. Your workspace paths, command invocations, and document counts remain entirely private.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="guarantee-card">
            <h3>🛡️ Share-Aware Visibility Controls</h3>
            <p>Every document can declare a <code>share: public | org | private</code> visibility key. Sensitive internal designs, architecture notes, and credential references marked <code>share: private</code> are automatically excluded from public exports.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Data Handling & Local Storage -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>2. Data Storage & Local State</h2>
        <p>
          ODS stores configuration and index files exclusively inside your local filesystem:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Workspace Indexes (<code>index.md</code>)</strong>: Generated directly inside your repository tree so they can be versioned with Git.</li>
          <li><strong>Global Configuration (<code>~/.ods/odsconfig.toml</code>)</strong>: Stores registered workspace paths and user preferences on your local disk.</li>
          <li><strong>Daemon IPC State</strong>: The background daemon (<code>ods serve</code>) uses OS-native local inter-process communication (IPC) or loopback sockets with zero public network listeners.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Visibility & Secrets Isolation -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>3. Secrets Isolation & <code>share: private</code> Policy</h2>
        <p>
          Modern documentation often coexists with internal operational details. ODS implements first-class visibility scoping in frontmatter:
        </p>
        <div class="code-block">
<pre><code>ods:
  profile: guide
  status: stable
  share: private  # Automatically excluded from 'ods share' and public AI context exports</code></pre>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong><code>share: public</code> (Default)</strong>: Standard documentation included in public site generators and public exports.</li>
          <li><strong><code>share: org</code></strong>: Restricts exports to internal organizational boundaries.</li>
          <li><strong><code>share: private</code></strong>: Strictly isolated. Excluded from <code>ods share</code> outputs and <code>ods context</code> dumps unless explicitly passed with <code>--include-private</code> in local execution.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: AI Assistants & LLM Integrations -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>4. Third-Party AI Models & IDE Integrations</h2>
        <p>
          When you use ODS with AI coding assistants (Claude Desktop, Cursor, VS Code, Zed, Windsurf, or Antigravity):
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>ODS acts as a local context provider. It generates bounded Markdown reading lists (<code>ods context &lt;id&gt;</code>) directly on your machine.</li>
          <li>ODS does not transmit your documentation to third-party AI providers. Any data sent to an LLM provider is governed strictly by your own AI client's privacy settings and API agreements.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: Updates & Version Checking -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>5. Updates & Version Checking</h2>
        <p>
          When running <code>ods update --check</code>, the CLI makes an anonymous HTTPS GET request to GitHub's public API (<code>api.github.com/repos/StaytunedLLP/open-document-specs/releases/latest</code>) solely to check if a higher version tag exists. No workspace data, repository contents, or user identifiers are included in this check.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6: Licensing & Contact -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>6. Licensing & Open Source Commitment</h2>
        <p>
          Open Document Spec core is open-source software licensed under the <strong>Apache License, Version 2.0</strong>. You are free to inspect, audit, modify, and self-host all ODS core components.
        </p>
        <p class="contact-info">
          For security inquiries or vulnerability reports, please visit our <a href="https://github.com/StaytunedLLP/open-document-specs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Repository</a> or contact <strong>Staytuned LLP</strong>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-container {
    width: 100% !important;
    max-width: 900px !important;
    margin: 0 auto !important;
    padding: var(--space-48) var(--space-20) var(--space-80) !important;
    box-sizing: border-box !important;
    overflow-x: hidden !important;
  }

  .privacy-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-32);
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .header-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.725rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: var(--nested-card-bg);
    color: var(--fg);
    border: var(--border);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-16);
    max-width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    white-space: normal;
    word-break: break-word;
  }

  .badge-dot {
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #22c55e;
    box-shadow: 0 0 8px #22c55e;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .privacy-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 5vw, 3rem) !important;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-16);
    line-height: 1.25;
    word-break: break-word !important;
    overflow-wrap: break-word !important;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  .privacy-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-24);
    word-break: break-word;
  }

  .meta-pills {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 8px;
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .meta-pill {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.725rem;
    padding: 4px 10px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--card-bg);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    border: var(--border);
    max-width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    word-break: break-word;
  }

  .privacy-divider {
    border: none;
    border-top: var(--border);
    margin: var(--space-32) 0 var(--space-48);
  }

  .privacy-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-48);
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .policy-section {
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .policy-section h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 3.5vw, 1.5rem) !important;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-16);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: var(--border);
    word-break: break-word !important;
    overflow-wrap: break-word !important;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  .policy-section p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-16);
    word-break: break-word;
  }

  .policy-section ul {
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-16);
    padding-left: 1.25em;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }

  .policy-section li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    word-break: break-word;
  }

  .guarantee-cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-16);
    margin-top: var(--space-20);
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .guarantee-card {
    padding: var(--space-16);
    background: var(--card-bg);
    border: var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    box-sizing: border-box;
    width: 100%;
    overflow-x: hidden;
  }

  .guarantee-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .guarantee-card p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .code-block {
    background: var(--code-bg);
    border: var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-16);
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: var(--space-16) 0;
    max-width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .code-block pre code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.825rem;
    color: var(--fg);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .contact-info {
    margin-top: var(--space-16);
  }

  .contact-info a {
    color: #58a6ff;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .privacy-container {
      padding: var(--space-24) var(--space-12) var(--space-48) !important;
    }
    .privacy-title {
      font-size: 1.6rem !important;
    }
    .privacy-subtitle {
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }
    .policy-section h2 {
      font-size: 1.2rem !important;
    }
    .guarantee-cards {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .meta-pills {
      gap: 6px;
    }
    .meta-pill {
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      padding: 3px 8px;
    }
  }
</style>
